---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import {
  STORED_WHEN_ACCOUNTS_SHIP,
  K_ANON_PUBLISH_FLOOR,
} from "../lib/storageDisclosure";
---
<Layout title="Privacy — Civic Ledger">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-neutral-700">
    This page describes what this site collects about you and what each thing
    is used for. It is a description, not a list of promises. The first half is
    what is true today. The second half is what accounts and email alerts will
    collect once they are built — written now, before any of it exists, so the
    description comes first and the collection second.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">What is collected today</h2>
  <ul class="mt-2 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-neutral-700">
    <li>
      There is no account system yet, so the site itself keeps nothing about
      you. Every page is static, built ahead of time from a dataset the
      operator maintains.
    </li>
    <li>
      The site is delivered by Cloudflare. Like any company that delivers a
      website, Cloudflare receives the requests your browser makes and keeps
      its own server logs of them, which it reports back to the operator as
      counts. That is a record of your reading, it is used to see whether the
      site is up and how much it is being read, and it is outside the
      operator's control.
    </li>
    <li>
      Reading the record needs no account. Every bill, topic and member also
      has a feed you can follow in a feed reader without signing up for
      anything. A feed reader polls on a schedule, so following a feed is a
      recurring request pattern in those same server logs.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">What will be collected when accounts ship</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    Accounts, email alerts and profiles are planned, not built. None of this
    exists yet and nothing below is being collected today. When they arrive,
    the site will hold these things about you, for these reasons, and
    <strong>the operator can read all of them</strong>:
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-2 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-neutral-700">
    {STORED_WHEN_ACCOUNTS_SHIP.map((thing) => <li>{thing.text}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    This describes what the features need. It is not a guarantee that nothing
    else is ever kept. If the list grows, this page is rewritten before the
    thing that grew it ships.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Your profile is the part other people can see</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    Everything else in that list is between you and the operator. A profile is
    the exception, and it is off until you turn it on: there is an explicit
    publish step, and <strong>anything you choose to publish on your profile
    is public</strong> — readable by anyone, and by anything that crawls the
    web. Nothing reaches a profile by default.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Deleting your account</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    Deletion is real deletion. Asking for your account to be deleted removes
    its rows across every one of the things listed above, rather than flagging
    them as hidden. Leaving an alert list is separate and simpler: every email
    carries an unsubscribe link that works without logging in.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Who else sees it</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    Cloudflare, the same company that delivers this site, is also the company
    that will send the email. It therefore receives your email address and the
    text of every message sent to you, and it keeps its own records of that,
    which can be demanded from it directly. Email is the only alert channel
    being built. A phone number, and the phone company that would carry the
    message, only come into it if text alerts are ever added — and that is not
    decided.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Numbers published about readers</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    No figure on this site today is drawn from what readers do, because
    nothing is collected about readers today. If one is ever published — how
    many people follow a bill, say — the rule it has to clear is written down
    already: it is published only if it covers at least {K_ANON_PUBLISH_FLOOR} people. Below
    that it is not published, because a small enough group is a group someone
    can be picked out of.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    The <a href="/threat-model" class="underline hover:text-neutral-900">threat model</a>
    is the long version of this page: what someone could learn about you, and
    what a legal demand would produce.
  </p>
</Layout>
